.TH DD-METRIC-BILL 1 "November 2026" "dd-metric-bill 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dd-metric-bill \- estimate the number of billable Datadog custom metrics in a sample
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
Usage: dd-metric-bill [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
Usage: dd-metric-bill count [OPTIONS] <SAMPLE>...
Usage: dd-metric-bill diff [OPTIONS] <OLD> <NEW>
Usage: dd-metric-bill completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Estimate the number of billable Datadog custom metrics in a sample.
.PP
The top-level help lists three commands.
.TP
.B count
Count billable custom metrics in one or more samples.
.I SAMPLE
is a sample file. \- reads standard input. At least one sample is required.
.TP
.B diff
Compare two samples.
.I OLD
is the old sample. \- reads standard input.
.I NEW
is the new sample. \- reads standard input.
.TP
.B completions
Print a shell completion script on standard output.
.I SHELL
is bash or zsh. The other options are accepted and ignored.
.PP
.nh
Contracts with Metric Name pricing are not supported.
Only count accepts --explain, --plan, --hosts, --allow-tags, --prices and --unbounded-threshold.
--hosts only works together with --plan.
--untyped-as only works together with --format prometheus.
.hy
.PP
The same options are printed by
.BR dd-metric-bill\ --help ,
by
.BR "dd-metric-bill count --help" ,
and by
.BR "dd-metric-bill diff --help" ,
except
.BR --version ,
which only the top-level help lists.
Passing an option that count accepts and diff does not accept makes diff exit 3, before it reads a sample or a price file.
.PP
Each sample and each price file may be at most 268435456 bytes (256 MiB).
Standard input has the same limit.
A larger input exits 2 and is not loaded.
The message says
.B file is larger than 268435456 bytes .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --format \fIFORMAT\fR
Input format: dogstatsd, jsonl or prometheus. The default is dogstatsd. Possible values: dogstatsd, jsonl, prometheus.
.TP
.B --json
Write the output as JSON.
.TP
.B --explain
Show the rule and the source for each metric. Only count accepts this option.
.TP
.B --hosts \fIN\fR
Number of hosts for the allotment. Only count accepts this option, and only together with --plan.
.TP
.B --plan \fIPLAN\fR
Plan for the allotment: pro or enterprise. Possible values: pro, enterprise. Only count accepts this option.
.TP
.B --histogram-aggregates \fIN\fR
Number of histogram aggregates per tag combination. The default is 4.
.TP
.B --histogram-percentiles \fIN\fR
Number of histogram percentiles per tag combination. The default is 1.
.TP
.B --percentiles
Include percentiles for distribution metrics.
.TP
.B --allow-tags \fILIST\fR
Comma-separated tag keys that may be indexed. Only count accepts this option.
.TP
.B --prices \fIFILE\fR
Path to a price file (JSON). Only count accepts this option.
.TP
.B --budget \fIN\fR
Fail if the number of custom metrics is above N. For diff, N is compared with the new total.
.TP
.B --top \fIN\fR
Number of tag keys in the breakdown.
.TP
.B --unbounded-threshold \fIN\fR
Unique values above N mark an unbounded tag. The default is 50. Only count accepts this option. On diff, passing the flag is rejected even when the value is the default.
.TP
.B --untyped-as \fIKIND\fR
Count Prometheus metrics without a type as gauge or count. Possible values: gauge, count. This option only works together with --format prometheus.
.TP
.B --quiet
Hide the hint line, even when stderr is a terminal. No context line.
.TP
.B --verbose
Print the hint line even when stderr is a pipe, and on success one context line on stderr.
.TP
.B --output \fIPATH\fR
Write the report to this file instead of standard output. An existing file is replaced. A missing parent directory is an error and is not created. Count and diff accept this option. The completions command ignores it.
.TP
.B -h , --help
Print help. Exit 0 when the help text can be written.
.TP
.B -V , --version
Print version. Exit 0 when the version text can be written. Shown by the top-level help only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was printed, or written to the file named by --output, or help or version was printed. With --budget, the total (for diff, the new total) is not above N.
.TP
.B 1
--budget was exceeded. The report is still printed on standard output, or written to --output when that flag is set. Standard output stays empty when --output is set. Standard error is one line: budget exceeded: TOTAL > LIMIT.
On a terminal, or with --verbose, a second line starts with hint:.
A pipe, a redirect, or --quiet keeps the one line.
.TP
.B 2
The sample or the price file cannot be read or is invalid, or the report cannot be written. A file larger than 268435456 bytes is this code. A failed report write does not panic.
.TP
.B 3
Usage error, including an unknown option, a missing argument, or an option combination the help text rejects. Standard output is empty. --help and --version that cannot be written also exit 3, and that failure does not panic.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT. The report is not left half-written. An existing output file is kept when the new report was not finished. Standard error is "interrupted by SIGINT".
.SH EXAMPLES
Count the fictional DogStatsD sample shipped in this repository. The default format is dogstatsd, so --format is not required. The exit code is 0.
.PP
.nf
.B dd-metric-bill count examples/page.dogstatsd
.fi
.PP
The three help texts, and the version. Each exits 0 when it can be written.
.PP
.nf
.B dd-metric-bill --help
.B dd-metric-bill count --help
.B dd-metric-bill diff --help
.B dd-metric-bill --version
.fi
